{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Context read that bears on framing rather than on the mechanism: the captured CHANGELOG's newest section is UNRELEASED after 1.7.0, and it contains no entry for RestoreCommittedLogs or the commit-tracking store interface, although both are documented in the captured Config and LogStore sources. That is recorded as a limitation on the parent account so a reader knows the affected configuration is an in-development opt-in feature rather than a released one; it does not weaken the finding, because the contract the account relies on is the documented one in the captured source. No evidence, comparison or conclusion changes.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-changelog\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"CHANGELOG.md\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1,\\\"end_line\\\":25,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"680bc27c9c50448a8b63097d98091061-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"680bc27c9c50448a8b63097d98091061-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\",\\\"s-dispatch-stage\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-runfollower-gate\\\",\\\"s-config-doc\\\",\\\"s-commit-tracking-contract\\\",\\\"s-installsnapshot\\\",\\\"s-changelog\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"5e1ce9aa430842d5a9325cfecbc885f6\\\":[0,1],\\\"e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9\\\":[0,1],\\\"183f75213c5a4f26a951f76784b3e54f\\\":[15,16],\\\"5627b36f50384d14851e4b5da991fa96\\\":[30,31],\\\"e1f5bf19d9fa482380acf68d58ec197e\\\":[32],\\\"3044e4e1ae284cf8abc323990e968c5c\\\":[33]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Six receipts of the same harness file answer this question. Two state the gap in clusters (5e1ce9aa430842d5a9325cfecbc885f6 and e1ee764584564a95b3e288381dfb75d9, each at its own indices 0 and 1), one states the gap for a hand-built history in a monotonic commit-tracking store (e1f5bf19d9fa482380acf68d58ec197e at index 32), one states the negative control where the snapshot already covers the change (3044e4e1ae284cf8abc323990e968c5c at index 33), and two state the repair paths (183f75213c5a4f26a951f76784b3e54f at 15 and 16, 5627b36f50384d14851e4b5da991fa96 at 30 and 31).\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled a restarted node does not load the committed configuration entries at or below the commit index it recovers; the mechanism is store-independent, the trigger boundary is measured in both directions, and both repair paths are measured. Mechanism: restoreFromCommittedLogs clamps the store's commit index, applies the recovered range through processLogs (which ends with setLastApplied), and the scan then starts at max(lastSnapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1, so a configuration entry at or below that index never reaches processConfigurationLogEntry; the snapshot loaded by restoreSnapshot is used as-is, which is why a cadence that snapshots past the change avoids the gap. Evidence and the consequences measured under it are as recorded in the child questions. Framing: the option and its store interface are documented in the captured Config and LogStore sources but have no entry in the captured CHANGELOG, whose newest section is UNRELEASED after 1.7.0, so the affected configuration is an in-development opt-in feature rather than a released one.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The negative control shows the gap is conditional, not universal: when the node's snapshot already covers the change, the restart recovers the configuration in force.\\\",\n    \\\"Both repair paths are measured: an arriving configuration entry restores the full set while the node is still a member, and an installed snapshot restores it when log replication is impossible.\\\",\n    \\\"The gap reproduces for a commit-tracking store that is also marked monotonic, so it is not an artefact of the store's indexing shape.\\\",\n    \\\"No captured test asserts configuration state after a RestoreCommittedLogs restart, so the captured suite neither contradicts nor covers this path.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Applies to nodes configured with RestoreCommittedLogs=true and a LogStore implementing CommitTrackingLogStore; with the flag off, lastApplied equals the snapshot index and the scan range is unchanged.\\\",\n    \\\"All measurements use in-memory stores (including a hand-built monotonic commit-tracking store) with the repository's in-memory transport and mock FSM; production stores are not measured.\\\",\n    \\\"The installed-snapshot repair needed the leader's log to have been compacted past the node's last index, which the probe arranged by letting the cluster commit eighty entries while the node was down; other ways of reaching that state are not measured.\\\",\n    \\\"The option has no entry in the captured CHANGELOG, whose newest section is UNRELEASED after 1.7.0, so this affects an in-development opt-in feature; the contract the accounts rely on is the documentation in the captured Config and LogStore sources.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
